# .trivyignore — the ONLY CVE escape hatch for the L4 security gate (Story 14.4 / ISI-2245, §6.2).
#
# This file is reviewed like code. Every suppression MUST carry, on the comment line directly
# above the CVE id:
#     <CVE-ID>   expires:YYYY-MM-DD   justification:<one line why this is accepted>
#
# The security.yml "trivyignore expiry lint" step FAILS the build when an entry is past its
# `expires:` date — a suppression is never a silent, perpetual mute. Remove or re-justify it
# before it expires. An unfixable finding still needs an entry (Trivy runs --ignore-unfixed, but
# a fix landing upstream turns a previously-unfixable HIGH into a gating one, so track it here).
#
# Format reference: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# --- active suppressions (none) ---
# (add entries below, newest first, each preceded by its expires:/justification: comment line)
